Self-Guitar content licence
===========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Self-Guitar contributors

Lessons, exercises and curriculum
---------------------------------
The lessons (content/lessons/), exercises (content/exercises/), warm-up
routines (content/warmups/), the curriculum
(content/curriculum.ts) and the chord library data (content/chords.ts) are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
License (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You may share and adapt them for any purpose, provided you give appropriate
credit ("Self-Guitar contributors", with a link to the project), indicate if
changes were made, and distribute your contributions under the same licence.

Song arrangements
-----------------
The song arrangements (content/songs/*/score.atex and song.cho) are dedicated
to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Each song's meta.json states this in its "license" and "attribution" fields.

Exception: imported scores (meta.json has "import"; arranger "Self-Guitar
(auto-fingered)") keep their source's licence, as stated in their meta.json:
an edition under CC BY or CC BY-SA (e.g. a Mutopia Project typesetting) stays
under that licence, with its typesetter credited, and so does the tablature
derived from it.

The underlying compositions are traditional or by composers who died long
enough ago that their works are in the public domain; each meta.json names the
composer and the source.

Contributing
------------
Only redistributable material is accepted here: public domain, CC0, CC BY,
CC BY-SA, or your own work offered under the licences above.
